# Accessibility and theme

- Target WCAG 2.2 AA: visible focus, keyboard reachability, labels/`aria-label` on icon-only controls, meaningful roles, contrast.
- Prefer semantic theme tokens / CSS variables from the design system. Avoid raw hex/RGB and one-off palette utility classes in product UI unless matching an existing tokenized pattern.
- Check light and dark themes for any UI change.
- Do not rename native HTML/React/Radix/shadcn/Inertia boolean props (`disabled`, `required`, `checked`, `open`, `defaultOpen`, `readOnly`, `asChild`, `preserveScroll`, `preserveState`, `replace`).
